  "headline": "Masoud Barzani and Mazloum Abdi discuss the future of Kurds in Syria",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "In Erbil, Masoud Barzani, President of the Kurdistan Democratic Party (KDP), received Mazloum Abdi, an adviser to the Syrian presidency, and a delegation to discuss Syria’s political developments and the future of Kurds in the country, according to the North Press Agency. The meeting, which took place on a Monday, reportedly focused on the political situation in Syria, the wider region, and predominantly Kurdish cities in north and northeast Syria (Rojava). Both parties emphasized the importance of stability, resolving outstanding issues, and dialogue. No further details regarding specific agreements reached during the meeting were provided. 1/1"
    }
  ]
